# Batch files must keep CRLF. A .cmd checked out with LF endings fails in ways
# that are hard to read -- goto and label handling in particular -- so pin it
# rather than leaving it to a contributor's core.autocrlf setting.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# The shell shim must keep LF for the same reason in reverse: a CRLF shebang
# line makes the kernel look for an interpreter with a trailing carriage return.
bin/loadout text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf
